---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Crumbs from '../components/Crumbs.astro';
import { countries } from '../data/countries';
const verified = countries.filter((c) => c.verifiedAt).length;
---
<Base title="How we check entry rules" description="Where Bemba's visa and health information comes from, how often it is checked, and how to report a change.">
  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <section class="page-head">
      <Crumbs items={[{ name: 'How we check', href: '/about/' }]} />
      <p class="eyebrow">Method</p>
      <h1 class="h1">How we check entry rules.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Bemba collects visa, vaccine and arrival rules for all 54 African countries in one place, with a link to the official source.</p>
    </section>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2 class="h2">Sources</h2>
      <p>We use government immigration portals, official eVisa sites, embassy pages and the World Health Organization's country list for yellow fever. Where a country has an official online portal, we link it on the country page.</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Verification status</h2>
      <p>Each country page shows whether its rules have been checked against official sources. Currently {verified} of {countries.length} countries are marked verified. Pages without that mark show a "being verified" notice.</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Updates</h2>
      <p>We review every country monthly and whenever a government announces a change. If a rule has changed and we have not caught it yet, email <span class="mono">hello@bemba.com</span> with the country and a link to the source.</p>
      <h2 class="h2">What Bemba is not</h2>
      <p>Bemba is a travel guide, not a visa agency, a lawyer or a doctor. We never charge for visas. Apply only on the official portal, and get medical advice from a travel clinic.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
